    "incident_id": "sheets-discovery-039",
    "outcome": "probable_cause",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "description": "Most likely cause: tool discovery truncation on cedar req-39. The returned googlesheets discovery page contained only 20 tools, indicated more pages, and explicitly shows the requested Sheets action was on a later page even though it still existed in the versioned catalog. This explains a missing action after discovery without requiring a provider-side failure.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_1b8d7225c1b0",
          "ev_fa5228b7ff1d",
          "ev_154da898e8ad"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [],
        "confidence": "high",
        "assumptions": [
          "The affected execution path depended on the observed first discovery page rather than completing pagination.",
          "The sandbox controlled comparison is supportive synthetic verification, not proof of a production change."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Less likely alternative: a broad provider failure/outage. This is weakened because the failed path is already explained before provider execution, provider reachability is reported healthy, and a comparison tenant shows same-window provider availability and a successful unrelated read.",
        "supporting_evidence": [],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_1b8d7225c1b0",
          "ev_63cc0806cce6",
          "ev_fa5228b7ff1d"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "If a broad provider outage were primary, comparable provider-facing failures or wider tenant impact would be expected in the supplied telemetry."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Secondary possibility: tenant-specific connection/configuration surface differences affected how discovery was performed or consumed. The controlled sandbox comparison says changing only 'sheets_configuration' flips the outcome, but there is no canonical production evidence here of grant loss, wrong account selection, revoked consent, or session-policy block for cedar req-39. This remains weaker than truncation.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_154da898e8ad"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_1b8d7225c1b0",
          "ev_63cc0806cce6"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "The reproduce record's 'sheets_configuration' variable may include client/config behavior beyond pure auth.",
          "A configuration difference could coexist, but it is not required to explain the observed missing-action-on-first-page mechanism."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "recommended_actions": [
      "Synthetic telemetry indicates a pre-provider discovery problem; proposed actions below have not been executed.",
      "Paginate googlesheets discovery for the affected path, or otherwise ensure later pages are retrieved before concluding the action is unavailable.",
      "If pagination cannot be completed in that path, evaluate increasing the discovery limit for the googlesheets toolkit and then use the exact returned action slug from the intended version.",
      "Capture and retain the full discovery payload, pagination state, and selected action slug for affected requests so production traces directly distinguish first-page omission from true catalog absence.",
      "Keep provider monitoring secondary for this incident path unless new canonical evidence shows requests reaching the provider and failing after discovery.",
      "Collect cedar-specific auth/session-policy/connection records for req-39 only if needed to rule in or out a tenant-specific configuration contributor."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Evidence is synthetic incident telemetry plus precomputed sandbox reproduction observations; reproduction records are supportive controls, not canonical production change records.",
      "No canonical record here includes the exact missing action slug string, only that the requested tool was on a later page and present in the version.",
      "No canonical cedar auth/session-policy event record is supplied for req-39, so stronger causal claims about wrong account, missing grant, or policy block would be speculative.",
      "No in-window tool-executor deployment was observed; this limits attribution to a timed internal code change."
    ]
  },
